    {
      "id": "W4GNb6L_1KSPAiQfEKpZt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3227.495449942699,
      "y": -97.69477294546311,
      "width": 2088.7114126947595,
      "height": 1610,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b68",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 18270146,
      "version": 1164,
      "versionNonce": 1674864541,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1743442981025,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design top k youtube videos by views\n\nFunctional requirements:\n\n1. Store the number of views categorized by a video\n2. Calculate the number of views in last minute, hour, day, week, minute or all-time\n3. Fetch the top k videos with largest number of views in last minute, hour, day, week, minute or all-time\n\nNon functional requirements:\n\n1. Low latency (< 100ms)\n2. Data integrity -> Should not lose any view or results in wrong calculation\n3. Scalability (1M TPS views)\n4. Max value for k - 1000\n5. As real time as possible\n6. Idempotency in storing views\n\nScale:\n\n    Assumptions\n    1. 100B views per day\n    2. 1M videos per day\n\n100B / 10^5 ~ 1M TPS views\n\nviews data -> 1M * 20 B - 20MB * 3650 ~ 100GB\n\nCore entities:\n\n1. View\nviewId\nvideoId: FK, video\nviewedBy: FK, User\ntimestamp\n\n2. Video\nvideoId\ntitle\ndescription\n...metadata\n\nAPIs:\n\n1. GET /api/v1/views/video?k={}&timestampFrom={}&timestampTo={}\n\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design top k youtube videos by views\n\nFunctional requirements:\n\n1. Store the number of views categorized by a video\n2. Calculate the number of views in last minute, hour, day, week, minute or all-time\n3. Fetch the top k videos with largest number of views in last minute, hour, day, week, minute or all-time\n\nNon functional requirements:\n\n1. Low latency (< 100ms)\n2. Data integrity -> Should not lose any view or results in wrong calculation\n3. Scalability (1M TPS views)\n4. Max value for k - 1000\n5. As real time as possible\n6. Idempotency in storing views\n\nScale:\n\n    Assumptions\n    1. 100B views per day\n    2. 1M videos per day\n\n100B / 10^5 ~ 1M TPS views\n\nviews data -> 1M * 20 B - 20MB * 3650 ~ 100GB\n\nCore entities:\n\n1. View\nviewId\nvideoId: FK, video\nviewedBy: FK, User\ntimestamp\n\n2. Video\nvideoId\ntitle\ndescription\n...metadata\n\nAPIs:\n\n1. GET /api/v1/views/video?k={}&timestampFrom={}&timestampTo={}\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
